      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(media-understanding): apply imageMaxDimensionPx resize to image description input (#101923)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #101923. The image description pre-processing pipeline passes images through at original dimensions without applying `agents.defaults.imageMaxDimensionPx`. Phone-camera photos exceed provider limits and fail:\n\n```\nImage dimensions exceed the 25,000,000 pixel input limit: 4536x8064\n```\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMoves the `resizeToJpeg` step into `normalizeImageDescriptionInput` — the shared image normalization function used by all image description paths. Only resizes when header metadata shows the image actually exceeds `maxSide`, avoiding unnecessary re-encoding of in-bounds images.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real behavior proof — resize only when oversized\n\n3000×3000 BMP → `resizeToJpeg(maxSide=2000)` → 2000×2000:\n\n```\n=== Before resize ===\nDimensions: 3000x3000 | bytes: 27000054\n\n=== After resizeToJpeg(maxSide=2000) ===\nDimensions: 2000x2000 | bytes: 69717\nWithin 2000px limit: true\n```\n\nImage already within limits → skipped (no unnecessary re-encode):\n\n```\nDimensions: 800x600 → maxSide=2000 → longerSide <= maxSide → skip resize\n```\n\n## Files Changed\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `src/media-understanding/image-input-normalize.ts` | +dimension check + `resizeToJpeg` when `maxSide` configured and image exceeds limit |\n| `src/media-understanding/runtime.ts` | Pass `resolveImageSanitizationLimits` → `maxSide` to `normalizeImageDescriptionInput` |\n",
        "branch": "fix/media-resize-ladder-bypass",
